            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "These docs are unformatted, and to a degree, outright unfished -- but I'd like to get some input before I put too much time going down a path that maybe folks won't think is that useful as-is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/hw_identification_daemons.md",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "If we move forward on this doc, I imagine updating this to include info on checking status on associated services and for seeing what's on each daemon's associated bus on D-Bus.\n\nie. \n\n> systemctl status xyz.openbmc_project.frudevice.service\n> journalctl -u xyz.openbmc_project.frudevice.service\n> busctl tree xyz.openbmc_project.FruDevice\n\ntype info"
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/hw_identification_daemons.md",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/my_first_sensors_troubleshooting.md",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "Apologies for such an ugly format-- but I wanted to get something out the door for early commentary, and didn't want \"good\" to be the \"enemy of getting started\"\n\nIf folks thing this doc is a good idea for Entity-Manager/docs, I'll get to work on making it look nicer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/my_first_sensors_troubleshooting.md",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "it's a bit hard to read with all the current formatting issues.  Could you fix it up quick?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/my_first_sensors_troubleshooting.md",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "On it.\n\nI was thinking today, that I'd work on filling in some gaps I left in the VPD daemons doc, then nice-up the format a bit before I post to ask for comments in the Sensors channel in the OBMC discord.\n\nI figure that'd be a good place to get comments from folks who might have some thoughts on this sort of sensors troubleshooting doc."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/my_first_sensors_troubleshooting.md",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "I went ahead and did a quick by-hand pass through the in-Gerrit text editor, and figure I'd post it sooner than later.\n\nDon't hesitate to nitpick the heck out of this thing -- I want it to be clear and as useful as possible for folks who might not know what's what with sensor readings (and the many components that come into play)\n\n\nI'll work on the VPD daemons next, then I'll probably give the 'main' doc another pass (and actually run it through a markdown visualizer) before I ask for input on Discord."
                }
            ],
