                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "To summarize chris and my discussion on discord:\n\"I fully support the concept of a debugging/troublshooting doc.  I don't think this review is valuable as it exists now until it's gone through.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "While I was thinking about \"how would this work as a pure troubleshooting doc\" (re: questions you asked on Discord), it occurred to me that a lot of the troubleshooting I personally did wouldn't be needed on most platforms -- and several of those issues I had got resolved with daemon-level changes anyways.\n\nCurrently I'm thinking about reframing this as a \"my_first_unsupported_sensor: a retrospective\" type doc that would be cleaned up with \"less is more\" -- as discussed on discord, but maybe retaining more of the existing structure the doc has now vs. what a true \"troubleshooting\" doc would be. \n\nIt would assume folks had already worked through the my_first_sensors doc, but maybe aren't sure to how to add something 'new' that no one else is using yet.\n\nWhat do folks think of approaching things from that angle?"
                }
            ],
